NAME
       pw_getpass, pw_lookup_name, pw_lookup_uid - account helpers

SYNOPSIS
       #include <pwutil.h>

       int pw_getpass(const char *prompt, char *buf, int cap);
       int pw_lookup_name(const char *name, uint32_t *uid, uint32_t *gid,
                          char *home, int home_cap, char *shell, int shell_cap);
       int pw_lookup_uid(uint32_t uid, char *name, int name_cap, ...);

DESCRIPTION
       pw_getpass reads a password with echo turned off and restores
       the terminal afterwards, including when interrupted.

       The lookup functions map between a user name and a numeric id
       and report the home directory and login shell.

       Checking a password is not done here: pass it to the kernel with
       cervus_auth, which compares it against the stored hash. See
       auth(2).

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       auth(2), su(1), passwd(1), login(1)
